add('thm-qftx-zero-fi-regular-adhm-asd-correspondence','Composition now uses actual Ward/local-frame/direct-image proofs,63–67 GAGA, independent68 two vanishings, Beilinson reconstruction and69 intrinsic real normal form, plus the exact raw forward block/charge conventions. This supplies the former A1 and analytic blockers while preserving N>=2, compact/framing actions, flat summands, raw moment signs and the exact first-order base-change range. Positive-FI Gieseker and ordinary zero-FI endpoints remain distinct.',old,integ,norm,pen,'root-analytic-integration-20261023/old60-range-root-receipt.json')
add('lem-qftx-rank-one-regular-adhm-and-ordinary-asd-boundary','Stabilization to rank2 preserves moments/stability/costability; the raw forward projection splits off a flat line, and independent determinant-flatness forces charge0. Ordinary ASD line emptiness/flat uniqueness uses determinant-flatness and simply-connected transport independently of inverse ADHM. Hermitian dual-number local lifts are made unitary, their imaginary cocycle is killed by partitions of unity, and Stokes plus H1(S4)=0 gives unique based gauge and zero tangent groupoids. Its exact rank2 prerequisites are now supplied; no positive-FI boundary is identified with ordinary ASD.', 'root-rank-one-review/review.json',integ,'root-analytic-integration-20261023/old60-range-root-receipt.json')
