add('def-qftx-gaga-coherent-section-topology','The definition now refers to actual surjective section presentations and is justified by the current quotient-topology lemma, whose canonical65 local acyclicity and Oka inputs are present. Separating seminorm completeness, presentation independence and restriction continuity are proved rather than inferred from sheaf epimorphisms; its definition/justification roles remain distinct.', 'batch66-cohomology-repair/review.md',fin)
add('lem-qftx-gaga-pseudoconvex-intersection-acyclicity','Finite intersections have actual psh exhaustions; componentwise regularization/Hartogs and the scalar Dolbeault resolution give ordinary O-acyclicity, including unbounded components. Oka partial free resolutions and the ordinary Euclidean bound dimension-shift coherent cohomology to zero; countable products are under full AC. Canonical65 and current metric-Cech support now supply the former stale/missing chain.', 'batch66-cohomology-repair/review.md',fin,local)
add('lem-qftx-gaga-coherent-section-topology-well-defined','Canonical65 local acyclicity gives the needed actual section surjections after shrinking. Finite jets plus Krull intersection close relation spaces; quotients are complete Frechet, matrix lifts make restrictions continuous, and compatible sections form a closed equalizer. Open mapping proves inverse gluing/presentation independence. Current Oka/65 and repaired Frechet/open-mapping proofs supply the former missing inputs.', 'batch66-cohomology-repair/review.md',fin,local)
